ere to say what are  some of the sort of most relaxing or  pleasing sounds I can imagine being a  completely untrained person in this  field I would  or to think about white noise machines  that are designed specifically for you  know a therapy session to make it hard  to hear what's going on or for sleeping  like I have when in my in my bedroom  ocean and water type noises and this can  include also like rain for example what  are first of all can you give us some  examples of the noises that are that are  known to be relaxing but then also like  how can we characterize them what are  their characteristics that we might  identify so I think that you know you  talk about the white noise machine I'm  gonna answer your question but you talk  about the white noise machine so I all I  think that sounds that we have control  over or more likely to be more pleasant  than anything so I think noise is sort  of like a proxy for control over our  environmental soundscape yeah so you  know I have a white noise machine around  tune when people come to visit me  they're like what is that that's like so  horrible sounding and they want me to  turn it off but like for me it's a way  that I can control my soundscape in my  apartment so to me it's it's not noise  it's sound but I think things that  people traditionally have found to be  pleasing would be like you said you know  natural sounding sounds that people like  silence to some people I found there's  like two camps people who just like no  sound at all  and then people were creeped out by  there and the people like music  classical music soothing things those  kinds of things  so let's talk about music a little bit  we we learned some years ago that one of  the so-called enhanced interrogation  techniques that was used in the Middle  East included not not just loud music  but specifically it seemed to be heavy  metal music that was being used so from  a obviously we can all have opinions  about heavy metal music and those might  differ but can you talk from a sort of  scientific perspective what is it that  makes heavy metal music of the style  that was used in these enhanced  interrogation techniques which some of  us call torture what makes it materially  different than other types of music I  think the frequency composition of it  you know this is just from this is my  opinion I don't know what types of  sounds they like what types of  heavy-metal music that uses these  interrogation techniques but you know  it's it's loud probably and it has like  this kind of high frequency pitch that's  like an annoying buzz in your ear I  don't know I grew up within the country  and I don't you know in the summertime  you would get mosquitoes that would fly  in your ear and when they would get  trapped it make this like high-pitched  sound and to me that's just completely  annoying so I'm assuming it's the pitch  probably higher pitches and then the  lower pitches as well the lower  frequencies that kind of constant  something in your chest over a period of  time and in my case my situation my  neighbors above me it drove me insane it  literally drove me insane last thing I  want to touch on is we have people who  listen to our show all over the country  but they are heavily concentrated in  places where lots of people live like  cities so I get emails from people about  upstairs noise noise outside all sorts  of stuff assuming you don't have a  budget to have professional sound  insulation and rooms within rooms built  and all of the stuff that would be done  professionally what what are like the  most effective sound mitigation  techniques that the average person in an  apartment can do white like masking it  so getting some sort of sound that  you're comfortable with that offsets it  so white noise machines I have a  soundtrack that sounds like you're  inside of an airplane so it has like a  rumbling because it keeps me from  hearing the footsteps above me in the  Train outside earplugs work 